5. The case of the claimant is that on 06.09.2006 he was travelling as a pillion-rider on a motorcycle to attend a function at Adavuladeevi of Repalle Mandal; on the way, the MACMA No.1820 of 2012 BVLNC, J Date 16.02.2024 motorcycle reached the place of accident located near Minenivaripalem;
the motorcycle, on which the claimant was travelling, was stopped in front of ditch to avoid falling into the ditch; another motorcycle bearing registration No.AP16AR 3679 (hereinafter referred to as 'offending motorcycle') driven by the respondent No.1 coming behind, dashed the motorcycle of the claimant, in a rash and negligent manner; as a result, the claimant fell down and sustained injuries;
the claimant was shifted to Repalle Hospital for First-Aid and again, he was shifted to a hospital at Guntur for better treatment; the claimant sustained seven (07) injuries out of which, six (06) are grievous in nature which includes head injury; the claimant has lost memory for twenty (20) days on account of the head injury; he spent a sum of Rs.50,000/- for his treatment; the hospital authorities informed the SHO, Guntur Town Police Station about the accident; the Guntur Police forwarded the information to Repalle Police; the Repalle police registered a case in Crime No.137 of 2006 for the offence punishable under Section 337 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 (for brevity 'IPC'); the respondent No.1 was MACMA No.1820 of 2012 BVLNC, J Date 16.02.2024 having valid driving licence; the respondent No.2 is the owner of the offending motorcycle; the respondent No.3 is the Insurer of the offending motorcycle and Insurance Policy was valid and in force at the time of accident; hence, the claim petition was filed claiming compensation for the injuries sustained by him in a motor vehicle accident.

